Changes in version 0.99.8

* Address Bioconductor review: combine the two vignettes into a single
  BiocStyle vignette with introduction, installation section, table of
  contents and a SummarizedExperiment integration example.
* Add BiocType field and BiocStyle to Suggests.
* Add examples to all exported help pages.
* Use internal accessors instead of direct slot access; vectorize genomic
  query dispatch, print method and per-row metadata conversion.
* Check for user interrupts in long-running C++ loops.
* Fix overlaps on circular sequences such as MT. Ranges that run past the
  end of a circular sequence now wrap around, matching GenomicRanges.
* Rewrite README and vignette text, and refresh benchmark results.
* Remove developer scripts (benchmark.R, build.sh) from the repository.

Changes in version 0.99.7

* Use one native genomic index per chromosome with strand filtering in C++.
* Store genomic row IDs and strands as native metadata rather than R objects.
* Update genomic construction and query benchmarks for the shared index.

* Rename the genomic class and constructor to SuperIntervalMap.
* Update overlap methods, conversion, examples and benchmarks to the new name.

Changes in version 0.99.6

* Root metadata in an R-owned list to avoid expensive per-value preservation
  and cleanup for large indexes.
* Add SuperIntervalMap, an S4 genomic subject index that preserves source
  GRanges and supports chromosome-aware and strand-aware overlap methods.
* Return Hits in original input row order and support standard GenomicRanges
  overlap options, with fallback for zero-width ranges and advanced options.
* Add a real airway RNA-seq annotation workflow and genomic integration tests.
* Validate against R 4.6 and Bioconductor 3.24 development dependencies.

Changes in version 0.99.5

* Synchronize generated Rcpp bindings and help files with SuperIntervals 1.0.3.
* Correct external-pointer finalizers and preserve metadata per stored occurrence.
* Validate coordinates at construction and mutation, and reject multi-sequence
  GRanges unless filtered. Keep query paths free of index-state checks.
* Use inclusive coverage widths and widened arithmetic in boundary operations.
* Document sorted indices, reference semantics, metadata policies and genomic
  coordinate limitations; add executable Bioconductor workflows and regression tests.
* Prepare package metadata, portable C++17 build files and submission guidance.

Changes in version 0.99.0

* Initial development version of the R wrapper for SuperIntervals.
